Third-party components, and which builds contain them
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Rubber Band Library — https://breakfastquay.com/rubberband/
  Copyright Particular Programs Ltd, trading as Breakfast Quay.
  GNU General Public License, version 2 or later. Full text: LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt
  (this project elects version 3 for the combination; see below).

  Present in: the macOS build only. Linked dynamically from Homebrew and embedded
  into the app bundle by App/embed-dependencies.sh.

  Absent from: every iOS and iPadOS build. Homebrew builds a macOS dylib and
  nothing else, so `CRubberBand` is a `.when(platforms: [.macOS])` dependency and
  the wrapper sits behind `#if canImport(CRubberBand)`. Verified on the artefact
  rather than assumed: the iPad build contains zero symbols matching "rubberband".

  **A binary that links Rubber Band is a combined work and may only be
  distributed under the GPL.** That is a fact about the binary, not about this
  source tree — see docs/LICENSING.md, which also records why the "or later" in
  Rubber Band's licence is load-bearing: Apache-2.0 is compatible with GPLv3 and
  is NOT compatible with GPLv2, so the combination must be taken as v3.

libsamplerate — https://github.com/libsndfile/libsamplerate
  Copyright (c) 2012-2016, Erik de Castro Lopo <erikd@mega-nerd.com>
  BSD 2-Clause License. Full text: LICENSES/BSD-2-Clause-libsamplerate.txt

  Present in: the macOS build only, and not because this project asked for it —
  librubberband links it, so App/embed-dependencies.sh copies both dylibs into
  Contents/Frameworks. It is a transitive dependency that is nonetheless
  genuinely shipped, and BSD-2-Clause requires the notice above to be reproduced
  in binary distributions, which is what this entry is for.

  Absent from: every iOS and iPadOS build, for the same reason Rubber Band is.

Signalsmith Stretch — https://github.com/Signalsmith-Audio/signalsmith-stretch
  Copyright (c) 2022 Geraint Luff / Signalsmith Audio Ltd.
  MIT License. Full text: LICENSES/MIT-signalsmith-stretch.txt

  Present in: every build, on every platform. Vendored as source under
  Sources/CSignalsmithStretch/vendor/ and compiled with the app rather than
  linked from a package manager, which is what allows it to exist on iOS at all.

  On iOS and iPadOS it is the only stretcher, and therefore the one that makes
  those builds a product rather than a demonstration.

Signalsmith Linear — https://github.com/Signalsmith-Audio/linear
  Copyright (c) 2025 Signalsmith Audio.
  MIT License. Full text: LICENSES/MIT-signalsmith-linear.txt

  Present in: every build. A separate repository from Signalsmith Stretch, which
  includes its FFT and STFT headers directly; it is vendored alongside for that
  reason and is not an optional component.

